   <text:h text:style-name="Heading_20_3" text:outline-level="3"><text:bookmark-start text:name="__RefHeading___Toc1304_1340120094"/><text:span text:style-name="T24">Accessibility Support</text:span><text:bookmark-end text:name="__RefHeading___Toc1304_1340120094"/></text:h>
   <text:p text:style-name="P37">The input fields in our GE graphs now have basic support for the ATK interface enabling various other tools like on-screen keyboards to work if the need arises. The events on focus and such are now fired and should be picked up by these tools.</text:p>
   <text:h text:style-name="P38" text:outline-level="3"><text:bookmark-start text:name="__RefHeading___Toc1306_1340120094"/>PMTU Discovery for UDP<text:bookmark-end text:name="__RefHeading___Toc1306_1340120094"/></text:h>
   <text:p text:style-name="P37">A new flag for setting the “Don’t Fragment” bit when using UDP has been added.</text:p>
   <text:h text:style-name="P38" text:outline-level="3"><text:bookmark-start text:name="__RefHeading___Toc1308_1340120094"/>New upgrade tool<text:bookmark-end text:name="__RefHeading___Toc1308_1340120094"/></text:h>
   <text:p text:style-name="P37">In an effort to try to make upgrading easier in the future we have moved to one tool named pwr_upgrade which combines the functionality of the upgrade.sh and reload.sh tools. The old tools are kept one version for overlapping reasons.</text:p>
   <text:h text:style-name="P38" text:outline-level="3"><text:bookmark-start text:name="__RefHeading___Toc1310_1340120094"/>Wireshark plugin for qcom in lua<text:bookmark-end text:name="__RefHeading___Toc1310_1340120094"/></text:h>
   <text:p text:style-name="P37">The wireshark plugin is now shipped as a lua file in addition to the old delivery where Wireshark had to be rebuilt. It is placed in <text:span text:style-name="T25">/usr/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu/wireshark/plugins </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T26">on a standard install on Debian, keep in mind that depending on distro/arch the path may be different. The name of the lua file is </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T25">packet-qcom.lua.</text:span></text:p>
   <text:h text:style-name="P39" text:outline-level="3"/>
   <text:h text:style-name="P40" text:outline-level="3"><text:bookmark-start text:name="__RefHeading___Toc1595_1340120094"/>RFC5424 Logging<text:bookmark-end text:name="__RefHeading___Toc1595_1340120094"/></text:h>
   <text:p text:style-name="P41">ProviewR will now log in RFC5424 format to make it easier for log pipelines to process logs from all process systems. The log viewer “System Messages” in rt_xtt still display log messages as one expects with the difference being that the filtering has been moved from menus to a toolbar.</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P41"/>
