      </office:binary-data>
     </draw:image>
    </draw:frame><text:line-break/><text:span text:style-name="T32">The advanced user can choose what steps to do. But hitting enter will go through all required steps. But as you might see the steps done after the version specific steps like compile PLCs and create loadfiles and such can be skipped if you prefer to do this manually later.</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P51">The upgrade tool will try to check the outcome of each step and stop if any fail, asking the user what to do.</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P51">When starting the steps you have the option to say “go” to just quickly execute them all. Otherwise you get to say y/n on each step. A new option “help” is also available that will tell you what the step does.</text:p>
   <text:h text:style-name="P12" text:outline-level="2"><text:bookmark-start text:name="__RefHeading___Toc1525_1340120094"/>1. Making a copy of the project<text:bookmark-end text:name="__RefHeading___Toc1525_1340120094"/></text:h>
   <text:p text:style-name="P32">This is optional but always recommended, as with everything we do, a backup is never a bad idea.</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P32">Do sdf to the project and start the administrator:</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P32"><text:span text:style-name="Source_20_Text"/></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P32"><text:span text:style-name="Source_20_Text">sdf project_name</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P32"><text:span text:style-name="Source_20_Text">pwra</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P32"/>
   <text:list text:style-name="L6">
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P52"><text:soft-page-break/>With the Project List opened, login as administrator if you lack access.</text:p>
    </text:list-item>
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P52">Enter edit mode and find the current project, <text:span text:style-name="T29">right click it,</text:span> and select Copy Project from the context menu of the ProjectReg object.</text:p>
    </text:list-item>
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P52">Open the newly copied object and assign a suitable project name and path.</text:p>
    </text:list-item>
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P52">Save and close</text:p>
    </text:list-item>
   </text:list>
   <text:h text:style-name="P33" text:outline-level="2"><text:bookmark-start text:name="__RefHeading___Toc1527_1340120094"/><text:span text:style-name="T13"><text:line-break/>2. Dump the databases</text:span><text:bookmark-end text:name="__RefHeading___Toc1527_1340120094"/></text:h>
   <text:p text:style-name="P53">Do sdf to the project if you haven’t.</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P53"><text:span text:style-name="Source_20_Text"/></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P53"><text:span text:style-name="Source_20_Text"><text:span text:style-name="T33">s</text:span></text:span><text:span text:style-name="Source_20_Text">df project_name</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P53"/>
   <text:p text:style-name="P53">Now execute the reload.sh script</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P53"/>
   <text:p text:style-name="P53"><text:span text:style-name="Source_20_Text">reload.sh</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P53"/>
   <text:p text:style-name="P53">It will say:</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P53"/>
   <text:p text:style-name="P53"><text:span text:style-name="Source_20_Text">Enter start pass [dumpdb] &gt; </text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P53"/>
   <text:p text:style-name="P53">Hit enter to execute the default starting step “dumpdb”. It will ask if you want to continue:</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P54"><text:span text:style-name="Source_20_Text"/></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P54"><text:span text:style-name="Source_20_Text">Do you want to continue ? [y/n/go] </text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P54"><text:line-break/>Say “y” here and press enter.</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P54"/>
   <text:p text:style-name="P53">The script will now dump the databases in the volume. <text:span text:style-name="T33">If by chance you get the error that the database is locked, you need to redo this step after making sure the database isn’t locked by someone.</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P55">The script then stops at the next step asking you if you want to continue. Choose n, as we don’t want to continue.</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P55">After that the script ends and we have our dump files.</text:p>
   <text:h text:style-name="P56" text:outline-level="2"><text:bookmark-start text:name="__RefHeading___Toc1529_1340120094"/>3. Changing the base version<text:bookmark-end text:name="__RefHeading___Toc1529_1340120094"/></text:h>
   <text:p text:style-name="P57">Enter the administrator <text:span text:style-name="T33">again, </text:span>and <text:span text:style-name="T33">locate your project in the Project List. C</text:span>hange the version of the project to V<text:span text:style-name="T33">7</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T34">.0.</text:span> <text:span text:style-name="T33">Note that since we have moved to semantic versioning we now only have the major and minor parts. </text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P57"><text:soft-page-break/>Save and close the administrator.</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P55">With the base changed for the project we can now issue sdf to the project once again to set everything up for the new version.</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P55"><text:span text:style-name="Source_20_Text"/></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P55"><text:span text:style-name="Source_20_Text"><text:span text:style-name="T32">s</text:span></text:span><text:span text:style-name="Source_20_Text">df project_name</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P55"/>
   <text:h text:style-name="P44" text:outline-level="2"><text:bookmark-start text:name="__RefHeading___Toc1531_1340120094"/>4. Do the actual upgrading<text:bookmark-end text:name="__RefHeading___Toc1531_1340120094"/></text:h>
   <text:p text:style-name="P41">If you want some information about the new tool check the section “The new tool”.</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P41">Once you have changed base to the new version and have done sdf to it execute <text:span text:style-name="T30">pwr_upgrade.sh</text:span>.</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P41"/>
   <text:p text:style-name="P41"><text:span text:style-name="Source_20_Text">pwr_upgrade.sh</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P41"/>
   <text:p text:style-name="P41">This will bring up the upgrade program. Without the <text:span text:style-name="Source_20_Text">--dump</text:span> argument the pwr_upgrade.sh tool starts in phase 2:</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P41"><draw:frame draw:style-name="fr4" draw:name="Image12" text:anchor-type="char" svg:width="16.999cm" svg:height="12.107cm" draw:z-index="16"><draw:image draw:mime-type="image/png">
